[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186115241 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" "question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/id #uuid "35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131713" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & -x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 4x-8y=4 \\\\  & -4x+8y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2y+1 \\\\ y=y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y+1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/id #uuid "5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16" "answer-d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76" "answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e" "answer-bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66" "answer-6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16" :answer/id #uuid "04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76" :answer/id #uuid "d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e" :answer/id #uuid "0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y+1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66" :answer/id #uuid "bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4" :answer/id #uuid "6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/id #uuid "0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/math-academy-id "q-131714" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+z=4 \\\\  & y-3z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-5z=2 \\\\  & y-3z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5z+2 \\\\ y=3z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5z+2 \\\\ 3z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/id #uuid "38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463" "answer-5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b" "answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef" "answer-e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3" "answer-75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463" :answer/id #uuid "8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2z+5 \\\\ z-3 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b" :answer/id #uuid "5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z+2 \\\\ 3z+1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef" :answer/id #uuid "5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z+2 \\\\ 3z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3" :answer/id #uuid "e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z-2 \\\\ 1-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33" :answer/id #uuid "75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/id #uuid "2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/math-academy-id "q-74636" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & -x+y=-1 \\\\  & 2x+3y=3 \\\\  & -x-4y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is inconsistent\n\nII. The system has a unique solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/id #uuid "eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc" "answer-33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521" "answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f" "answer-4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863" "answer-4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc" :answer/id #uuid "2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521" :answer/id #uuid "33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f" :answer/id #uuid "b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863" :answer/id #uuid "4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d" :answer/id #uuid "4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116493 :tutorial/content "We can use Gaussian elimination to find the general solutions of systems with any number of equations and variables. For instance, consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1, \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has the augmented matrix\n![](images/8a/8a8452587098eed9b697c3999c356359b949429f29ce16af2c81cf728be9480e.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\, & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable $z.$ From the second equation, we get $y=-3z,$ and from the first equation, we obtain $x=1-4z.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1-4z, \\\\ y=-3z, \\\\ z=z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/id #uuid "35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d"] ["question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131713"] ["question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & -x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 4x-8y=4 \\\\  & -4x+8y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] ["question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2y+1 \\\\ y=y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y+1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/id #uuid "5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6"] ["answer-04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16" :answer/id #uuid "04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16"] ["answer-04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76" :answer/id #uuid "d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76"] ["answer-d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e" :answer/id #uuid "0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e"] ["answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y+1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66" :answer/id #uuid "bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66"] ["answer-bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4" :answer/id #uuid "6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4"] ["answer-6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4" :answer/value "No solution"] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/correct "answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e"] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-04b4afa6-a500-5c42-b71e-8897fdf83e16"] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-d20192a2-17f7-5cf2-89ef-9364425f3c76"] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-0aee1394-8b26-588f-9a54-890e3d3e715e"] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-bfc2041b-d7a6-5f71-9c74-5af435e3fa66"] ["answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-6d65baaa-b447-55bf-9ca2-d0463511c9a4"] ["question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6"] [17592186115241 :knowledge-point/questions "question-35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d"] ["question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/id #uuid "0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86"] ["question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/math-academy-id "q-131714"] ["question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+z=4 \\\\  & y-3z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] ["question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-5z=2 \\\\  & y-3z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5z+2 \\\\ y=3z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5z+2 \\\\ 3z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/id #uuid "38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b"] ["answer-8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463" :answer/id #uuid "8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463"] ["answer-8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2z+5 \\\\ z-3 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b" :answer/id #uuid "5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b"] ["answer-5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z+2 \\\\ 3z+1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef" :answer/id #uuid "5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef"] ["answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z+2 \\\\ 3z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3" :answer/id #uuid "e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3"] ["answer-e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z-2 \\\\ 1-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33" :answer/id #uuid "75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33"] ["answer-75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33" :answer/value "No solution"] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/correct "answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef"] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/choices "answer-8f70eb8f-375f-50cc-a932-8c671ab51463"] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/choices "answer-5b91d99c-3ffc-59d0-9ca0-819cbe514f5b"] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/choices "answer-5037d6fc-9e95-53ff-8293-fe7f48a52eef"] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/choices "answer-e27eb335-12ff-5cee-84c6-5fa2be9c6ab3"] ["answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b" :answer-field/choices "answer-75022ec7-7eef-58e8-96f6-520f1f5efd33"] ["question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-38a28058-8837-5c47-bd4f-999f7f79529b"] [17592186115241 :knowledge-point/questions "question-0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86"] ["question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/id #uuid "2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891"] ["question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/math-academy-id "q-74636"] ["question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & -x+y=-1 \\\\  & 2x+3y=3 \\\\  & -x-4y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is inconsistent\n\nII. The system has a unique solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent"] ["question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] ["question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/id #uuid "eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6"] ["answer-2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc" :answer/id #uuid "2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc"] ["answer-2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521" :answer/id #uuid "33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521"] ["answer-33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f" :answer/id #uuid "b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f"] ["answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863" :answer/id #uuid "4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863"] ["answer-4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d" :answer/id #uuid "4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d"] ["answer-4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/correct "answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f"] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-2a116b39-7748-5b97-8286-409d809e42cc"] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-33822258-829b-5084-adb7-be68d8b35521"] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-b11d6ce5-b8fc-5e47-ad56-2ad45b30686f"] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-4eac203e-2b67-5cbd-b5f3-2f4c25980863"] ["answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" :answer-field/choices "answer-4ae92370-bb9c-5f64-acc7-34346d0fb34d"] ["question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6"] [17592186115299 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891"] [17592186116493 :tutorial/content "We can use Gaussian elimination to find the general solutions of systems with any number of equations and variables. For instance, consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1, \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has the augmented matrix\n![](images/8a/8a8452587098eed9b697c3999c356359b949429f29ce16af2c81cf728be9480e.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\, & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable $z.$ From the second equation, we get $y=-3z,$ and from the first equation, we obtain $x=1-4z.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1-4z, \\\\ y=-3z, \\\\ z=z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "retractions" [[17592186116493 :tutorial/content "We can use Gaussian elimination to find the general solutions of systems with any number of equations and variables. For instance, consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=1, \\\\ y+3z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system has the augmented matrix\n\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\, & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z &=1 \\\\ y+3z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe see that the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable $z.$ From the second equation, we get $y=-3z,$ and from the first equation, we obtain $x=1-4z.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1-4z, \\\\ y &=-3z, \\\\ z &=z.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"]]}]